Input: {"question": "When was the Delta Upsilon Fraternity House built?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d00", "start": 0, "end": 161, "text": "Delta Upsilon Fraternity House (Ann Arbor, Michigan) The Delta Upsilon Fraternity House is a fraternity house located at 1331 Hill Street in Ann Arbor, Michigan."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d00", "start": 162, "end": 228, "text": "It was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1995."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d00", "start": 229, "end": 314, "text": "Delta Upsilon was founded in 1834 at Williams College in Williamstown, Massachusetts."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d00", "start": 315, "end": 377, "text": "The chapter at the University of Michigan was founded in 1874."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d00", "start": 378, "end": 429, "text": "By the early 1900s, the chapter needed a new house."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d00", "start": 430, "end": 532, "text": "Alumni pooled donations, and the chapter hired Detroit architect Albert Kahn to design this new house."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d00", "start": 533, "end": 587, "text": "Construction began in 1902, and was completed in 1903."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d00", "start": 588, "end": 615, "text": "Delta Upsilon was the first"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d01", "start": 0, "end": 161, "text": "Delta Upsilon Fraternity House (Ann Arbor, Michigan) The Delta Upsilon Fraternity House is a fraternity house located at 1331 Hill Street in Ann Arbor, Michigan."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d01", "start": 162, "end": 228, "text": "It was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1995."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d01", "start": 229, "end": 314, "text": "Delta Upsilon was founded in 1834 at Williams College in Williamstown, Massachusetts."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d01", "start": 315, "end": 377, "text": "The chapter at the University of Michigan was founded in 1874."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d01", "start": 378, "end": 429, "text": "By the early 1920s, the chapter needed a new house."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d01", "start": 430, "end": 532, "text": "Alumni pooled donations, and the chapter hired Detroit architect Albert Kahn to design this new house."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d01", "start": 533, "end": 587, "text": "Construction began in 1920, and was completed in 1921."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d01", "start": 588, "end": 663, "text": "Delta Upsilon was the first to have a dedicated fraternity house on campus."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d02", "start": 0, "end": 200, "text": "Delta Upsilon Fraternity House (Champaign, Illinois) The Delta Upsilon Fraternity House is a historic fraternity house located at the University of Illinois at Urbana–Champaign in Champaign, Illinois."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d02", "start": 201, "end": 324, "text": "The house was built in 1926-27 for the university's chapter of the Delta Upsilon fraternity, which was established in 1905."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d02", "start": 325, "end": 467, "text": "In its early days, the fraternity was known for its academic success; early members included actor George Chandler and chemist Arnold Beckman."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d02", "start": 468, "end": 529, "text": "Architect Leonard Steube designed the Tudor Revival building."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d02", "start": 530, "end": 670, "text": "The house combines elements of the more formal types of Tudor Revival architecture, such as its brick gabled entrance and chimney with stone"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d03", "start": 0, "end": 120, "text": "Delta Upsilon Chapter House The Delta Upsilon Chapter House is a historic building located in Ames, Iowa, United States."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d03", "start": 121, "end": 243, "text": "It is considered one of the more imposing architectural examples among fraternity chapter houses at Iowa State University."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d03", "start": 244, "end": 296, "text": "It was designed by Des Moines architect Alexander M."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d03", "start": 297, "end": 371, "text": "Linn, who joined Delta Upsilon at what was then called Iowa State College."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d03", "start": 372, "end": 437, "text": "The fraternity's chapter house was on Hyland Avenue at that time."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d03", "start": 438, "end": 606, "text": "Linn, howevever, did not graduate from Iowa State as he transferred to the University of Illinois where he graduated with a degree in architectural engineering in 1923."}, "D4S7": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d03", "start": 607, "end": 625, "text": "Completed in 1930,"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d04", "start": 0, "end": 76, "text": "initiates may ever be admitted and even whose existence may be kept secret ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d04", "start": 77, "end": 265, "text": "The walls of the house may be decorated with pictures of past chapter events , awards , and trophies , decorative ( or historic ) paddles , or composite photos of members from past years ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d04", "start": 266, "end": 420, "text": "In some fraternities or sororities , only the representatives live in the houses while in others the entire fraternity or sorority may live in the house ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d04", "start": 421, "end": 527, "text": "Other , larger fraternities or sororities may have more than one house to accommodate all of its members ."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d04", "start": 528, "end": 546, "text": "At many colleges ,"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d05", "start": 0, "end": 12, "text": "and Beyond ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d05", "start": 13, "end": 53, "text": "Delta Upsilon International Fraternity ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d05", "start": 54, "end": 60, "text": "1991 ."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d05", "start": 61, "end": 90, "text": "^ Stevens , Albert ( 1907 ) ."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d05", "start": 91, "end": 123, "text": "The Cyclopædia of Fraternities ."}, "D6S6": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d05", "start": 124, "end": 129, "text": "E.B ."}, "D6S7": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d05", "start": 130, "end": 143, "text": "Treat and Co."}, "D6S8": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576:d05", "start": 144, "end": 146, "text": "p."}, "D6S9": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0492-52e21b7485